<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Consell de la Terra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1419</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Consell de la Terra ('Council of the Land') was the assembly of Andorra, created in 1419 when the co-princes allowed the parishes to send representatives to deal with common affairs. It developed into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/general-council-of-andorra">Consell General</a>, which from 1702 met in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/casa-de-la-vall">Casa de la Vall</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andorra-la-vella">Andorra la Vella</a>. It is regarded as one of the oldest parliaments in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> still in existence.</p></div>
